1.2.1.5 Labels, Arrows and Polygons
...................................

‘label’, ‘vector’ and ‘polygon’ take the same arguments as in the ‘draw’
package.  ‘label’ and ‘vector’ are drawn as Plotly annotations: they
never appear in the legend, and are not yet supported inside
‘animate(...)’ or in ‘ax_draw3d’.

ax_draw2d(
  polygon([[0,0], [2,0], [1,1.5]], fill_color="rgba(100,100,230,0.2)", line_width=0),
  label(["A", 0, -0.1], ["B", 2, -0.1], ["C", 1, 1.6], font_size=16),
  label(["slope", 0.45, 0.85], label_angle=56),
  vector([1, 0.2], [0, 0.6], color="red", head_both=true),
  aspect_ratio=true
)$

   • Label text may contain Unicode (‘"i⁺"’, ‘"𝓘⁻"’, ‘"ρ"’).  Use
     ‘font_size’, ‘font_color’ (defaults to ‘color’) and ‘font_family’
     to style it.
   • ‘label_alignment’ (‘left’ / ‘center’ / ‘right’) and ‘label_valign’
     (‘top’ / ‘middle’ / ‘bottom’) say which side of the text sits on
     the point.
   • ‘label_offset=[dx, dy]’ shifts the text by pixels (dy up), so it
     stays the same distance from its point whatever the axis ranges.
     With ‘label_valign=bottom’ and ‘label_offset=[0, 4]’ the text sits
     just above the point.
   • ‘label_angle’ rotates the text, in degrees counterclockwise;
     ‘label_orientation=vertical’ is the same as ‘label_angle=90’.
   • ‘vector’ uses ‘color’ and ‘line_width’ for the arrow, ‘head_size’
     (relative to the line width) and ‘head_style’ (Plotly arrowhead
     shape 0-8) for the head, and ‘head_both=true’ for heads at both
     ends.
   • ‘polygon’ fills with ‘fill_color’ and outlines with ‘color’,
     ‘line_width’ and ‘dash’; ‘line_width=0’ hides the outline and
     ‘transparent=true’ draws the outline only.


